YPE existing_study_type="Other"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>Artificial oxygenation can be used to restore oxygen-depleted coastal basins, yet key microbial responses and oxygen-consumption pathways remain poorly understood. The aim of this study was to investigate the initial consumption of oxygen and sulfides in Paddehavet during a reoxygenation experiment. Shotgun metagenomic sequencing was performed both on samples from a laboratory based oxygenation experiment, on samples from Paddehavet prior to oxygenation and after 4 months of oxygenation. Paddehavet is located in the Oslofjord (Norway). The project was carried out in collaboration with The Norwegian Institute for Water Research (NIVA) and funded by Hafslund.</STUDY_ABSTRACT></DESCRIPTOR></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="4C" accession="SRS28369268"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS28369268</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN56464316</EXTERNAL_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="pda|matildesterling@gmail.com" label="Sample name">4C</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>4C</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>749907</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>sediment metagenome</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><DESCRIPTION>4C - time 24 hours, day 1</DESCRIPTION><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>1426923</ID><LABEL>PRJNA1426923</LABEL></XREF_LINK></SAMPLE_LINK></SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>host</TAG><VALUE>not applicable</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>isolation_source</TAG><VALUE>marine sediment</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>collection_date</TAG><VALUE>not applicable</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>geo_loc_name</TAG><VALUE>Norway: Oslofjorden,Paddehavet</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>lat_lon</TAG><VALUE>59.874293 N 10.766674 E</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>source_material_id</TAG><VALUE>PD5</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>Sample_no</TAG><VALUE>12</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>BioSa